{"parameters":{"model":"dxn:com.anthropic.model.claude-opus-5.default","stream":true,"tools":[{"name":"eval","description":"Runs code against the workspace and returns whatever that code printed. This is the only tool: every read, every write and every operation happens inside it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string","description":"The program, in the dialect the system prompt describes. Print anything you need to see."}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":true}}]},"prompt":{"content":[{"options":{},"role":"system","content":"## Code mode\n\nYou have exactly one tool, `eval`. Its `code` is the body of an `Effect.gen` generator run\nagainst this workspace, so `yield*` is available and you must NOT write the wrapper yourself.\nIt returns whatever the code printed: a value you do not `print` never reaches you. Do not use\n`import` or `require` — the modules below are already in scope.\n\nPrefer one `eval` call that does the whole job — query, inspect, change, print — over a call\nper step. Print the specific values you need to reason about, not whole objects.\n\n### In scope\n\n- `Database`, `Filter`, `Query`, `Obj`, `Ref`, `Type`, `DXN`, `Operation`, `Effect` —\n  the DXOS modules, as a source file would import them.\n- `types` — every registered object type, keyed by typename:\n  `types['example.com/type/Task']`.\n- `print(...values)` — an effect: `yield* print('count', tasks.length)`. Strings go through\n  verbatim, everything else is printed as JSON.\n\n### Reading and writing\n\n```js\nconst tasks = yield* Database.query(Filter.type(types['example.com/type/Task'], { status: 'open' })).run;\nyield* print('open', tasks.length);\n\nObj.update(tasks[0], (task) => { task.status = 'done'; });\n\nconst created = yield* Database.add(Obj.make(types['example.com/type/Task'], { title: 'New', status: 'open' }));\nyield* Database.flush();\nyield* print('created', created.id);\n```\n\n`Obj.update` is synchronous and is the only way to change a stored object. `Database.remove`\ndeletes one. Call `Database.flush()` before printing a final confirmation.\n\n### Types\n\nEvery registered type and its fields. This is the whole schema — do not introspect it further.\n\n- `com.example.type.expando` — \n- `com.example.type.task` — title, status, priority\n- `org.dxos.type.feed` — name, kind, namespace, rewindFrom\n- `org.dxos.type.skill` — name, description, instructions, tools, agentCanEnable, mcpServers, hooks\n- `org.dxos.type.instructions` — name, description, input, output, text, skills, objects, commands\n- `org.dxos.type.function` — name, description, updated, source, inputSchema, outputSchema, services, binding, icon\n- `org.dxos.type.assistant.chat` — name, viewType, remote, feed, instructions, model, tasks\n- `org.dxos.type.trigger` — runnable, spec, enabled, remote, concurrency, inputNodeId, input\n- `org.dxos.type.tag` — label, hue\n- `org.dxos.type.alarm` — wakeAt, message, created\n- `org.dxos.type.view` — query, projection\n\n### Operations\n\nNo operations are bound to this conversation."},{"options":{},"role":"user","content":"Every task of type com.example.type.task whose title mentions docs must be closed: set its status to \"done\". Then tell me how many tasks are done in total."},{"options":{},"role":"assistant","content":[{"options":{},"type":"text","text":"I'll query the tasks, find those mentioning \"docs\", close them, then count all done tasks."},{"options":{},"type":"tool-call","id":"toolu_01ErkM7dumdRSMbBof13tZYt","name":"eval","params":{"code":"const tasks = yield* Database.query(Filter.type(types['com.example.type.task'])).run;\nyield* print('total tasks', tasks.length);\nyield* print('all', tasks.map((t) => ({ id: t.id, title: t.title, status: t.status })));"},"providerExecuted":false}]},{"options":{"anthropic":{"cacheControl":{"ttl":"5m","type":"ephemeral"}}},"role":"tool","content":[{"options":{},"type":"tool-result","id":"toolu_01ErkM7dumdRSMbBof13tZYt","name":"eval","isFai